// `int` was a bare alias for `int32` — a second spelling for a type that already had one, carrying no
// information of its own. It was removed rather than repurposed as the platform-width type: kama keeps
// the `size` in `isize`/`usize`, which is what says WHY they are distinct and why a crossing needs a cast.
// The diagnostic must name the replacement, not just report the absence — every pre-existing kama program
// and every C/Java-trained reader lands here.
fn int32 main() {
    int x = 5;
    return x;
}
